@lang en

-- us-ch2-repeals.l4 : Title 1, chapter 2, sections 108 to 111 (what a repeal does).
-- Source: usc01.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text); quotation lines copy it.
--
-- Each function is named for what the section PROVIDES, so FALSE reads "the section does not provide this", not "the
-- opposite happens". Where an input is "expressly so provided", the input is a fact about the text of the instrument
-- (a witness can read it), and which instrument has to provide it is a fork in NOTES.md (F-108).
--
-- Title 1 has no rule on repeal and re-enactment, and none on what a repeal does to things done under the repealed
-- text beyond the three cases in sections 109, 110 and 111. Those two silences are named refusals at the end.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Chapter 2 - Repeals`

§§ `Section 108 - Repeal of repealing act`

-- src:102 | Whenever an Act is repealed, which repealed a former Act, such former Act shall not thereby be revived, unless it shall be expressly so provided.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 108 (src:102)
GIVEN `revival is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 108 provides that the former Act is not revived by the repeal of the repealing Act` `revival is expressly provided` MEANS
    NOT `revival is expressly provided`

§§ `Section 109 - Repeal of statutes as affecting existing liabilities`

-- src:106 | The repeal of any statute shall not have the effect to release or extinguish any penalty, forfeiture, or liability incurred under such statute, unless the repealing Act shall so expressly provide, and such statute shall be treated as still remaining in force for the purpose of sustaining any proper action or prosecution for the enforcement of such penalty, forfeiture, or liability.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 109, first sentence (src:106)
GIVEN `incurred under the repealed statute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `released expressly by the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 109, repeal: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` `incurred under the repealed statute` `released expressly by the repealing Act` MEANS
        `incurred under the repealed statute`
    AND NOT `released expressly by the repealing Act`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 109, first sentence (src:106)
GIVEN `incurred under the repealed statute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `released expressly by the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 109, repeal: the repealed statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` `incurred under the repealed statute` `released expressly by the repealing Act` MEANS
    `section 109, repeal: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` `incurred under the repealed statute` `released expressly by the repealing Act`

-- src:106 | The expiration of a temporary statute shall not have the effect to release or extinguish any penalty, forfeiture, or liability incurred under such statute, unless the temporary statute shall so expressly provide, and such statute shall be treated as still remaining in force for the purpose of sustaining any proper action or prosecution for the enforcement of such penalty, forfeiture, or liability.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 109, second sentence (src:106)
GIVEN `incurred under the temporary statute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `released expressly by the temporary statute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 109, expiration: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` `incurred under the temporary statute` `released expressly by the temporary statute` MEANS
        `incurred under the temporary statute`
    AND NOT `released expressly by the temporary statute`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 109, second sentence (src:106)
GIVEN `incurred under the temporary statute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `released expressly by the temporary statute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 109, expiration: the temporary statute is treated as still in force to sustain a proper action or prosecution to enforce it` `incurred under the temporary statute` `released expressly by the temporary statute` MEANS
    `section 109, expiration: the penalty, forfeiture or liability is not released or extinguished` `incurred under the temporary statute` `released expressly by the temporary statute`

§§ `Section 110 - Saving clause of Revised Statutes`

-- src:110 | All acts of limitation, whether applicable to civil causes and proceedings, or to the prosecution of offenses, or for the recovery of penalties or forfeitures, embraced in the Revised Statutes and covered by the repeal contained therein, shall not be affected thereby, but all suits, proceedings, or prosecutions, whether civil or criminal, for causes arising, or acts done or committed prior to said repeal, may be commenced and prosecuted within the same time as if said repeal had not been made.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 110 (src:110)
GIVEN `embraced in the Revised Statutes and covered by the repeal in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 110: the act of limitation is not affected by the repeal` `embraced in the Revised Statutes and covered by the repeal in it` MEANS
    `embraced in the Revised Statutes and covered by the repeal in it`

-- Second limb of the sentence. It reads "all suits, proceedings, or prosecutions ... for causes arising, or acts done or
-- committed prior to said repeal", and is encoded on those words alone (fork F-110 in NOTES.md). The time itself, "the
-- same time as if said repeal had not been made", is the time the repealed act of limitation allowed, and Title 1 does
-- not state it, so the function says only whether the rule applies.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 110 (src:110)
GIVEN `cause arose or act done before the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 110: the suit, proceeding or prosecution may be commenced and prosecuted within the same time as if the repeal had not been made` `cause arose or act done before the repeal` MEANS
    `cause arose or act done before the repeal`

§§ `Section 111 - Repeals as evidence of prior effectiveness`

-- src:114 | No inference shall be raised by the enactment of the Act of March 3, 1933 (ch. 202, 47 Stat. 1431), that the sections of the Revised Statutes repealed by such Act were in force or effect at the time of such enactment: Provided, however, That any rights or liabilities existing under such repealed sections shall not be affected by their repeal.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 111 (src:114)
GIVEN `repealed by the Act of March 3, 1933` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 111 forbids the inference that the section was in force or effect when the Act of March 3, 1933 was enacted` `repealed by the Act of March 3, 1933` MEANS
    `repealed by the Act of March 3, 1933`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 111, the proviso (src:114)
GIVEN `repealed by the Act of March 3, 1933` IS A BOOLEAN
      `existing under the repealed section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 111, proviso: the right or liability is not affected by the repeal` `repealed by the Act of March 3, 1933` `existing under the repealed section` MEANS
        `repealed by the Act of March 3, 1933`
    AND `existing under the repealed section`

§§ `What the text does not provide: repeal and re-enactment, and things done under the repealed text`

-- Searched: ss 1-8, 101-114, 201-213. "repeal" occurs only in ss 108 to 111 (and the chapter heading). Nothing in them treats
-- a repeal that is accompanied by a re-enactment of the same text, and nothing says what a repeal does to a right, an
-- act done, a proceeding begun or a privilege, other than the cases above.
@ref 1 U.S.C. ss 108-111 are the only sections on repeal; none speaks to repeal and re-enactment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Title 1 has no rule on whether a thing done under the repealed text keeps its effect after a repeal and re-enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Title 1 has no rule on whether a thing done under the repealed text keeps its effect after a repeal and re-enactment"

@ref 1 U.S.C. ss 108-111 are the only sections on repeal; none speaks to rights, acts done or proceedings begun beyond the cases above
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Title 1 has no general rule on what a repeal does to a right, act done or proceeding begun under the repealed text beyond sections 109 to 111` MEANS
    REFUSE "Title 1 has no general rule on what a repeal does to a right, act done or proceeding begun under the repealed text beyond sections 109 to 111"
